{%- comment -%}
  Resolves one variant to a single customer-facing state. Echoes exactly one of:

    own        in our own stock          → fastest, green
    partner    only at a partner         → slower, amber
    available  sellable, source unknown  → green, but promises no lead time
    none       cannot be bought          → grey

  The point of the split is that "where" is an internal fact and "when" is the
  customer's question. Callers turn these into a delivery expectation; nobody
  ever sees a location name.

  `available` is the honest degraded state. It happens when Shopify says the
  variant is sellable but the metafield has nothing for it — Flow not run yet, a
  brand-new product, or the sweeper mid-cycle. Claiming "ships in 1-2 days" there
  would be inventing a promise, so the lead time is simply omitted and the chip
  falls back to plain "In stock". With the metafield absent entirely the whole
  page degrades to exactly the old in/out behaviour.

  `variant.available` is authoritative for sellability: if Shopify will not sell
  it, no metafield entry can override that to anything but `none`. The metafield
  only ever refines a yes into own-vs-partner.

  Accepts:
  - variant: {Object} variant object

  Usage:
  {%- capture state %}{% render 'variant-stock-state', variant: variant %}{% endcapture -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign vss_state = 'none'

  if variant.available
    assign vss_ns = settings.stock_metafield_namespace | default: 'custom'
    assign vss_key = settings.stock_metafield_key | default: 'stock_by_location'

    assign vss_entries = variant.metafields[vss_ns][vss_key].value
    if vss_entries == blank
      assign vss_entries = variant.product.metafields[vss_ns][vss_key].value
    endif

    comment
      Keys are wrapped in pipes so a location named "Recharge" cannot match
      "Recharge Partner" by substring.
    endcomment
    assign vss_primary = settings.stock_primary_locations | default: 'Recharge'
    assign vss_primary = vss_primary | newline_to_br | replace: '<br />', ',' | replace: '<br>', ','
    assign vss_primary_list = vss_primary | split: ','
    assign vss_primary_keys = '|'
    for name in vss_primary_list
      assign clean = name | strip | downcase
      if clean != blank
        assign vss_primary_keys = vss_primary_keys | append: clean | append: '|'
      endif
    endfor

    assign vss_own = false
    assign vss_partner = false

    for entry in vss_entries
      assign entry_name = entry.name | strip | downcase
      if entry_name == blank
        continue
      endif

      assign entry_in = false
      if entry.available == true
        assign entry_in = true
      else
        assign entry_qty = entry.quantity | plus: 0
        if entry_qty > 0
          assign entry_in = true
        endif
      endif
      unless entry_in
        continue
      endunless

      assign needle = '|' | append: entry_name | append: '|'
      if vss_primary_keys contains needle
        assign vss_own = true
      else
        assign vss_partner = true
      endif
    endfor

    comment
      Free fallback that lights up on its own if local pickup is ever enabled —
      see the Stock by Location notes in CLAUDE.md for why it is empty today.
    endcomment
    unless vss_own or vss_partner
      for availability in variant.store_availabilities
        unless availability.available
          continue
        endunless
        assign avail_name = availability.location.name | strip | downcase
        assign needle = '|' | append: avail_name | append: '|'
        if vss_primary_keys contains needle
          assign vss_own = true
        else
          assign vss_partner = true
        endif
      endfor
    endunless

    if vss_own
      assign vss_state = 'own'
    elsif vss_partner
      assign vss_state = 'partner'
    else
      assign vss_state = 'available'
    endif
  endif

  echo vss_state
-%}
